<title>USA: Teva wins FDA OK for hypertension drug.</title>
<headline>Teva wins FDA OK for hypertension drug.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said Friday that the Food and Drug Administration has given it approval to make and sell 2.5 mg Indapamide tablets.</p>
<p>The tablets are a generic equivalent of a Lozol, a drug made by Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc to treat hypertension, the company said.</p>
<p>The announcement follows one earlier this week, when Teva said it received FDA approval to make and market Nicardipine, a generic version of Cardene from Roche Laboratories.</p>
<p>Teva makes and markets branded and generic pharmaceuticals. It is Israel's largest pharmaceutical company.</p>
